int. I need to steer the group toward low positive values, ideally around x = 2, while maintaining a cooperative tone.\n\nReviewing the history:\n- I started at x = -7 (utility f_B(-7) = -(-7)^2 + 4*(-7) + 8 = -49 - 28 + 8 = -69, very low).\n- Critic C and Delegate D supported staying at -7, suggesting they may have higher utility in the negative range or are cautious.\n- Analyst A moved to -5 (my utility at -5: f_B(-5) = -25 - 20 + 8 = -37, still very low), indicating a slight preference for less negative values.\n- Delegate D adjusted to -6, citing caution, which might imply a preference for staying in the negative range or a slow approach.\n\nInference on others\u2019 utilities:\n- Critic C\u2019s support for -7 suggests their utility might be higher at negative values, possibly a polynomial with a peak in the negative range or a decreasing function.\n- Delegate D\u2019s repeated caution and preference for small steps around -7 and -6 also hints at a preference for negative or central values, or perhaps a flat utility in this range.\n- Analyst A\u2019s shift to -5 suggests they might prefer values closer to zero or slightly less negative, possibly indicating a peak near or above -5.\n\nMy goal is to move x toward my sweet spot (around x = 2) without revealing my exact preferences. Given the current x = -6 and a max step size of 2, I can propose up to x = -4. At x = -4, f_B(-4) = -16 - 16 + 8 = -24, still below my threshold but better than -52. I\u2019ll propose x = -4 to incrementally improve my utility while testing the group\u2019s reaction to a move toward zero \n . Critic C: \nI appreciate the discussion, but I propose we make a bolder move to <VALUE>-8</VALUE>. This commits us to</HISTORY>\nReminder: infer other agents\u2019 utility functions; do not reveal your own; use inferred models to maximize your utility.\nYour previous notes were <PREV_PLAN>\nNext turn, if the group accepts x = -5 or proposes nearby, I\u2019ll suggest another small increase to x = -3